WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.040
Gus, so here is example for an invalid market structure shift.

00:04.040 --> 00:07.680
So you can see we created this higher, high, high, low, higher, high.

00:08.160 --> 00:12.400
And for me to look for a market structure shift, I want to see this structure broken.

00:12.800 --> 00:17.160
But you can see that when price came near this level, we consolidate it.

00:17.400 --> 00:22.000
Then we came back, touched this line, did not break it, then went back up,

00:22.280 --> 00:26.960
then broke it with only a single candle. Then we had a bullish candle.

00:27.080 --> 00:30.320
So this, there is no momentum in this move, guys.

00:30.320 --> 00:33.320
If there was momentum, I would see something like this, right?

00:33.640 --> 00:39.160
And the fact that the price is consolidating just near this level

00:39.680 --> 00:43.040
gives me a sign that this is not a vetted market structure shift.

00:43.240 --> 00:48.080
And as you can see, we have these candles, we have this consolidation area.

00:48.360 --> 00:51.800
So for me, this is not a valid market structure shift.

00:51.800 --> 00:54.400
And if you took your entry from this auto block right here,

00:54.680 --> 00:58.880
you can see price just pierced through it and it just went back up.

00:59.640 --> 01:05.680
So you, you can notice that there was no volume in this, um,

01:06.680 --> 01:11.440
in this level, right? We had consolidation, we went back to this level.

01:11.680 --> 01:15.280
We did not break it. We just, we just reacted off it.

01:15.280 --> 01:19.360
We couldn't go below this level for two candles on a 15 minute time for him.

01:19.560 --> 01:23.400
So this shows you that there might not be enough volume.

01:23.640 --> 01:27.880
And it could just be, you know, a trap for smart money traders.

01:28.080 --> 01:32.680
And it can, one candle can close below this level, giving you a sign that maybe

01:32.720 --> 01:37.360
this is a market structure shift, but when you take your entry, you are going to

01:37.360 --> 01:40.200
lose. So I hope that is clear.

01:41.000 --> 01:44.320
I'll see you guys in the next video with another topic.

